            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for to respect, then the Italian for the integration."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: il partito",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "il partito — \"the political party\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Non sono iscritto a nessun partito. I am not a member of any party."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also the past participle of partire: è partito."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "partito is the past participle of partire in its old sense \"to divide\", inherited from Latin partīrī \"to divide\", from pars, partis \"a part\" (Lewis & Short): one part of the people."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
